prompt.en:
A teacher makes five cards and writes the whole numbers 1 to 31 on them by these rules (a number may appear on several cards):
Card A: numbers with remainder 1 when divided by 2;
Card B: numbers with remainder 2 or 3 when divided by 4;
Card C: numbers with remainder 4, 5, 6 or 7 when divided by 8;
Card D: numbers with remainder 8 to 15 when divided by 16;
Card E: the numbers 16 to 31.
An thinks of a whole number from 1 to 31 and finds that it is on cards B, C and E but not on cards A and D. What is his number?
